        "body": "The most common isolation bug in application code is not an exotic anomaly. It is this pattern: read to check a condition, then write based on the answer. Take a sign-up form. The code runs `SELECT 1 FROM users WHERE username = 'sam'`; if no row comes back, it runs `INSERT INTO users ... 'sam'`. Run two requests for the same name at the same moment and both checks see nothing, because neither insert is visible yet, and both inserts then go through.",
        "diagram": "sequenceDiagram\n  participant A as Request A\n  participant DB as Database\n  participant B as Request B\n  A->>DB: SELECT username = sam, no rows\n  B->>DB: SELECT username = sam, no rows\n  A->>DB: INSERT sam\n  B->>DB: INSERT sam\n  Note over DB: both succeed, two users named sam",
